{"type":"standard","title":"Cumanagoto language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Cumanagoto language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q5193784","titles":{"canonical":"Cumanagoto_language","normalized":"Cumanagoto language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Cumanagoto language</span></span>"},"pageid":36204877,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/129-Imagen-2653-1-17-20200613.jpg/330px-129-Imagen-2653-1-17-20200613.jpg","width":330,"height":227},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/10/129-Imagen-2653-1-17-20200613.jpg","width":975,"height":671},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1353697594","tid":"776a4dbf-4d7a-11f1-9083-0df7702659d5","timestamp":"2026-05-11T20:46:21Z","description":"Extinct Cariban language of Venezuela","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cumanagoto_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cumanagoto_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cumanagoto_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Cumanagoto_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cumanagoto_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Cumanagoto_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cumanagoto_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Cumanagoto_language"}},"extract":"Cumanagoto, also Itoto Majun, Palank, Pariagoto or Tamanaku is an extinct Cariban language of eastern coastal Venezuela. It is the language of the Cumanagoto people and other nations. Extinct dialects include Palenque, Piritu (Piritugoto), and Avaricoto.","extract_html":"<p><b>Cumanagoto</b>, also Itoto Majun, Palank, Pariagoto or Tamanaku is an extinct Cariban language of eastern coastal Venezuela. It is the language of the Cumanagoto people and other nations. Extinct dialects include <i>Palenque</i>, <i>Piritu</i> (<i>Piritugoto</i>), and <i>Avaricoto</i>.</p>"}